 CellChangeTimes->{{3.991421011498423*^9, 3.991421019951182*^9}, {
  3.991421823425428*^9, 
  3.99142183503187*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b8f32c55-c082-418a-84e5-\
a78d58e8e573"],

Cell["\<\
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]The estimated DSNB flux is 3.6 \[PlusMinus] 1.6 cm\
\:207b\.b2 s\:207b\.b9, consistent with the range predicted by several \
theoretical models (for example, the Horiuchi et al. 2009 6 MeV model, which \
predicts 2.1\[Dash]3.9 cm\:207b\.b2 s\:207b\.b9).\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]SK observed the first indication of the DSNB. The \
best-fit DSNB signal flux obtained from
a joint fit of SK-Ntag era phases (SK-IV, V, VI, VII, VII.5, VIII) is 3.6 \
+1.6/-1.5 cm-2 s-1 (4.8 +2.2/-
2.0 events yr-1) for E > 13.3 MeV, assuming the Horiuchi+09, 6 MeV, max \
model. This
corresponds to a 2.6\[Sigma] tension with a null hypothesis (5x10-3 one-sided \
p-value). Similar
significance was obtained for two other DSNB models with varying spectral \
shapes.\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.991422235735723*^9, 3.991422237293109*^9}, {
  3.991422279232456*^9, 
  3.991422283008802*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"60a34d9a-e36a-4e7e-810c-\
7a68a1297b0b"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"3.6", "+", "1.6"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"3.6", "-", "1.5"}]}], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.991422606965015*^9, 3.9914226130776663`*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[846]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ed717589-b081-4e01-888a-251a2316116d"],

